## Problem
[`crates/raw/src/preview.rs#L405-L412`](https://github.com/storytold/lightcraft/blob/31ee2643cf208a18cf780b8a63c677e87ab256f7/crates/raw/src/preview.rs#L405-L412) computes `j + len` and `start + size` from 32-bit box fields cast to `usize`, checks them, then does `&bytes[j..j + len]`. On wasm32 (`usize` = 32 bits) a length near `u32::MAX` wraps, both checks pass, and the slice panics; the web profile is `panic = "abort"`. Reached through `embedded_preview` (import fallback and thumbnails) for CR3 files whose track parse finds no JPEG. Not reachable on 64-bit release builds.

## Suggested fix
```diff
- if len < 4 || j + len > start + size.max(24) || j + len > bytes.len() { continue; }
- let jpeg = &bytes[j..j + len];
+ let (Some(end), Some(lim)) = (j.checked_add(len), start.checked_add(size.max(24))) else { continue };
+ if len < 4 || end > lim { continue; }
+ let Some(jpeg) = bytes.get(j..end) else { continue };
```

## Regression test
On an i686/wasm32 target, a buffer with a `PRVW` box whose JPEG length is near `u32::MAX` returns no preview without panicking.

